A||||6||Klown||Air dam question||||5||
Z||000000||Klown||05-27-2000||07:48 PM||||I noticed that the black plastic air dam underneath the radiator of my fiero is broken (probably from hitting those little parking barriers all the time!)  My question is what is this thing for and do I really need it?  I was thinking of just pulling it off but I wasn't sure if I needed to replace it afterwards.  ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-27-2000||08:21 PM||||Well its an air dam, do you think it was placed there for looks?<P>You need it to keep the front of the car down when you drive over 60 mph, otherwise, you'll be on the back two wheels as the front lifts, because that thing is missing.||||reg||12
Z||000002||TOM||05-27-2000||09:50 PM||||or its there to direct air up through the radiator. With out it you MAY get some overheating problems. Some cars will and some wont.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||05-27-2000||09:52 PM||||I dont know about the Fiero, but an 86 Trans Am with out the air dam WILL overheat at highway speeds! The air dam is there for a reason other than appearance.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||05-27-2000||11:52 PM||||Would anyone know where I can find one? New or used. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000005||Klown||05-28-2000||12:18 AM||||Thanks guys.  I tend to think it helps direct air up into the radiator also.  I guess I'll be making a trip to salvage yard to look for one that's in decent shape.  Or maybe I'll just take it off so that Old Lar and other people can see me pop wheelies down the highway! ||||reg||12
Z||000006||rogergarrison||05-28-2000||06:45 AM||||yes its there to push more air into radiator. You can use any you can find in junkyard all camaros , firebirds have em, even if there a little too long-cant hurt. As far as air dams, rear wings etc, making your car handle better----keep dreaming, they dont do a thing except look cool unless your going over 150 mph. (well maybe the rear wing will help keep dust and dirt off the taillites)||||reg||1
